module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.call_expression_erased_at_v2_body_lowering

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data call_expression_erased_at_v2_body_lowering: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "call_expression_erased_at_v2_body_lowering" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a call expression is erased by v2 normalize before resolve runs, so every reference it carries -- callee and arguments -- is invisible to name resolution and the refusal a missing declaration should raise has nothing to fire on** (INVALID STATE: v2.compiler.normalize, via v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold, lowers a function body that is a call into a Transform node whose only child is the `dag_token_lbrace` atom. The callee identity and every argument subtree are dropped. The module then passes normalize and resolve Accepted, with no diagnostic of any severity).",

    "HARM. v2 name resolution failed OPEN for the whole call-expression population while lowering dropped the call: a name no declaration provides was Accepted. The namespace cut's census rests on a delete-first premise, that removing an authority makes every real dependent REFUSE LOUDLY, and that premise is void for every dependent reached through an erased call. Interpreter prepared/unprepared now refuse the enrolled undeclared-callee specimen at resolve; native census mode still performs no resolution and cannot establish binding-refusal completeness. A native run with no passing call-bearing identities does not by itself identify lowering as the cause of every refused identity.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS, because two neighbouring rows look like this one and are not. `unresolved_callee_conflated_with_dispatched_elsewhere` is the v1 ExprCall-tail class: there the callee reaches the classifier and the miss is absorbed later. AT FILING (2026-09-12 interpreter dumps), the v2 callee never reached resolve at all: the earlier dated measurements (v2.test.claim.dag_acceptance frontier_arm_note, and a since-deleted staged_front_end commentary row) attributed the silence to resolve, which was the wrong stage — resolve is correct over the tree it receives, and that tree had already lost the call, so a resolve-side wall would have been a decoration because the undeclared-callee RED and the declared-callee positive control arrived as identical trees. THAT IDENTITY IS NO LONGER THE INTERPRETER FACT: those two trees now differ, and the resolve-side assertion is executing evidence rather than a decoration. Native remains unshown.",

    "RECEIPT (2026-09-12, still-eagle-447, NAMESPACE XL-2 scoping). The normalized tree was dumped for five bodies via prepare_grammar, parse_module_prepared and normalize -- the calls v2.compiler.program_assembly program_assembly_read_to_normalized_root_prepared makes, and so the census route's own hand-off (v2.compiler.compile native_test_context_from_ingest). `{ k }` keeps `Atom:k`. `{ x }` over a parameter keeps `Atom:x`. `{ g(x: 1) }` with g declared, `{ zzz(x: 1) }` and `{ zzz(1) }` with zzz undeclared all become `Transform [ Atom:dag_token_lbrace ]`. The unprepared parse_module route (v2.compiler.staged_front_end run_front_end) dumps identically, so this is not a second lossy route beside a faithful one.",

    "EVIDENCE LEVEL, stated so the receipt is not read one rung high. The dumps ran the v2 .dag through the gunbc interpreter at main f9d37e43a1, and a structural node-count fold (not a printer) agrees: the parse tree grows with a call's arguments and nesting, while the normalized body of { g(x: 1) } is exactly one node larger than { k } -- the Transform and its lbrace atom -- and { g(x: h(y: 5)) } is no larger than that. A second named argument adds one node, so the lowering keeps something per extra argument, but none of the callee or argument content. That the natively emitted normalize behaves identically is not executed. The native route gives no contrary evidence: its receipt on the #10940 head (eager-raven-113, 2026-09-12) holds exactly one Passed identity, a literal-bodied smoke test, and every richer body refuses before or at eval (v2.compiler.infer node_grounding_frontier_note). So no route has been observed to lower a call faithfully.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: the minimum across in-scope paths (DESIGN section 4b). Interpreter prepared and unprepared: mechanically preventable — undeclared callee refuses at resolve with resolve_reason_unbound_symbol, and enrolled argument-subtree controls RED if erasure is restored. Native realization of a declared argument-dependent call is not executed here, so the class rung remains that path: outside the ladder until arm (i) lands.",

    "CEILING: structurally guaranteed. Whether a name is bound in the containment index is decidable, and v2 resolve already refuses an unbound VALUE name with `resolve_reason_unbound_symbol`. The missing piece is not an authority but the lowering preserving what resolve needs.",

    "PARTIAL CLIMB (2026-09-14, #11322). Interpreter prepared and unprepared now preserve enrolled call shapes. Arm (ii): undeclared callee refuses at resolve with resolve_reason_unbound_symbol (v2.test.claim.staged_front_end staged_front_end_unbound_value_name_refuses_with_its_own_reason, including undefined_callee_zzz). Arm (iii): v2.test.manual.body_lowering_projection_call body_lowering_normalize_accepts_projection_module — postfix helper.step(a, b) keeps callee step at arity 2; the same identity also normalizes `{ g(x: 1, y: 0) }` and `{ g(x: h(y: 5), y: 9) }` (two calls named g, inner h under outer g, some g at arity 2). Restoring erasure or the flat-comma peel that dropped the argument after a nested call reds that identity. Arm (i) is not delivered: a declared callee through the native route returning an argument-dependent result is unexecuted on this head.",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, naming the residual capability: a call with a DECLARED callee executes through the NATIVE route and returns the expected ARGUMENT-DEPENDENT result, so the argument subtree is carried and consumed rather than merely present on that path. Interpreter prepared/unprepared arms (ii) and (iii) do not stand in for native. A census count or a migration of known call sites does not fire this trigger.",

    "CENSUS CONSEQUENCE, recorded because the cut consumes it: the whole-tree native census (the emitted closure binary's census mode) runs only tokenize, parse and normalize per file and never calls resolve, so its roster carries front-end refusals only. Restoring call lowering does not by itself add resolve refusals to that census. That needs the census mode to resolve per module as well.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
